WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:15.520
JULIE (PROVIDER): Hi, I'm Julie, the speech therapist. Before we begin,
I want to show you CareScribe and the five parts of today's visit.

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:17.960
DEB (CAREGIVER): I'm Deb. I'm the mom.

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:24.280
BYRON (SIMULATED CHILD ROLE): I'm acting as the child in the room.
I will make random noises rather than speak.

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:30.440
DEB: Do I need to take notes during this visit
to make sure I can take care of my son?

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:43.880
JULIE: No. CareScribe will keep a summary. We'll review case history,
play, and communication, then make a plan together.

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:46.480
[SIMULATED CHILD VOCALIZATION]

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:50.080
JULIE: That's okay. We'll give them time to settle in.
They don't need to perform for me.

00:00:52.120 --> 00:01:02.400
JULIE: I'll ask about pregnancy, birth, early development, health,
and daily life. Were there any pregnancy complications or concerns?

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:06.520
DEB: No major complications. I was monitored more closely near the end.

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:11.120
JULIE: How was the birth? Were they near their due date?
Did they need any extra care?

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:16.000
DEB: Just a little early. We all went home together
and didn't need to stay in the hospital longer.

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:32.320
DEB: Sorry, I'm trying to remember. Did you ask about other milestones?
JULIE: You're getting ahead of me, and that's fine. Take your time.

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:39.320
JULIE: What age did they start walking?
When did you first notice communication sounds?

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:42.320
[SIMULATED CHILD VOCALIZATION]

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:57.320
DEB: They walked a little after their first birthday.
He points to tell us what he wants, but doesn't use many words.

00:01:57.320 --> 00:02:02.320
JULIE: What happens when they want something
during a familiar routine such as snack time?

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:07.320
DEB: They usually take my hand and lead me to the kitchen.

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:17.320
JULIE: That helps me understand communication at home.
CareScribe is organizing development and daily life as we go.
